# Requests to the api for the REST Client extension. No secrets in this file.
# Start the api first (`bb dev`, or `(go)` in the REPL). To call protected endpoints, run
# `bb token <username>` (or `bb token scheduler`) in a terminal and paste the result into
# @token below; access tokens last 5 minutes. Demo users: see tools/realm.clj.

@api = http://localhost:4000
@token =

### Liveness: the process is up
GET {{api}}/healthz

### Readiness: Keycloak's signing keys and the FHIR server answer (503 when one does not)
GET {{api}}/readyz

### Who am I: identity, roles and the FHIR resource that is me
GET {{api}}/api/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Without a token: 401 and a bare WWW-Authenticate challenge
GET {{api}}/api/me

### The panel: the patients the caller may see (a practitioner's panel, everyone for the admin)
GET {{api}}/api/patients
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Filter by family name (a prefix, any case, accents ignored), sort and page
GET {{api}}/api/patients?family=garcia&sort=birthDate&limit=10&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One patient's demographics: your own, one on your panel, or anyone for the admin
GET {{api}}/api/patients/pt-ana
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A patient that does not exist: 404 for staff, 403 for a patient (no way to probe)
GET {{api}}/api/patients/pt-ghost
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### With a bad token: 401 and error="invalid_token"
GET {{api}}/api/me
Authorization: Bearer not.a.token

### A request id of your own comes back on the response and in the logs
GET {{api}}/healthz
X-Request-Id: my-trace-1

### A route that does not exist: 404 as application/problem+json
GET {{api}}/nope

### A method the route does not support: 405 with Allow
POST {{api}}/healthz
